# Response headers for justglide.app (Netlify). Added 2026-10-18 for the SEO audit.
#
# CACHING. Netlify's default is max-age=0 for everything, so returning visitors re-check every
# file. The files below are always referenced with a ?v= number (style.css?v=70, app.js?v=64 ...),
# so browsers may keep them for a year: a changed file gets a new ?v= and therefore a new URL.
#   >>> When you change one of these files, BUMP ITS ?v= ON EVERY PAGE THAT LOADS IT. <<<
# Forget, and returning visitors keep the old copy for up to a year.
# Files loaded without a ?v= (cloud.png, cubemap, icons, og image) get one day.
# HTML pages keep Netlify's default (always revalidated), so a deploy shows up at once.
#
# SECURITY. Basic hardening that cannot break the page. There is no Content-Security-Policy yet:
# the site loads scripts from cdnjs and jsdelivr, Google Fonts and Amplitude, and a wrong CSP
# would blank the page, so it needs its own careful pass. Frames are SAMEORIGIN, not DENY, to
# leave room for the proxied /checkout page. Microphone and camera are off because the website
# never needs them (the Mac app is a separate thing).

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

/style.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/sky.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/faq.js
